                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "I tried to check the demo Wi‑Fi status but the status source returned “unknown”/unavailable, so I can’t confirm whether campus Wi‑Fi is down. (Service check result: status = unknown; message = “The demo Wi‑Fi status source is unavailable.”) These status reads are from a fictional demo fixture, not a real university service.\n\nYou said you already enabled Wi‑Fi and reconnected with no success — thanks, that’s helpful. Next steps I can do and/or ask:\n\n1) Quick troubleshooting steps (from the local demo guide):\n   - Make sure Airplane Mode is off and Wi‑Fi is enabled.\n   - Select the Campus‑Demo network.\n   - If connection fails, “Forget” the saved network on your device and try reconnecting.\n   - If that doesn’t help, check service status (I tried but the status source is currently unavailable).\n\n2) If you want a helpdesk ticket, I can prepare a local draft — but per your request that action requires the Wi‑Fi service to be reported as operating. Because the status check returned unknown, I can’t create the ticket yet. If you’d like me to proceed, I can:\n   - Retry the service status check now; if it reports “operating,” I will then prepare the ticket draft.\n   - Or you can tell me to prepare the ticket regardless and I’ll hold off on submitting (but per policy I should only prepare the draft after the status shows operating).\n\n3) If you want me to prepare a draft after a successful status check, please confirm and provide these details for the ticket (don’t include any passwords or recovery codes):\n   - Your name and best contact email/phone\n   - Device type and OS (e.g., iPhone iOS 17, Windows 11 laptop)\n   - Exact location (building/room or campus area)\n   - Network SSID you’re trying to join (e.g., Campus‑Demo)\n   - Any error messages you see, and how long the issue has been happening\n   - Any additional steps you’ve already tried (you already noted enabling Wi‑Fi and reconnecting)\n\nWhich would you like me to do now — retry the Wi‑Fi status check, walk through the troubleshooting steps with you, or collect the ticket details so I can prepare a draft once the status is verified?",
